+// Root CA trust store for outbound HTTPS (Grammana Z / grammar LLM calls
+// and Google Drive sync). Without this the ESP32 does TLS but never
+// verifies the server, so a network attacker could impersonate the
+// endpoint and capture the API key and file contents.
+//
+// Contents: Google Trust Services (GTS R1-R4), GlobalSign, DigiCert,
+// USERTrust/Comodo, Go Daddy/Starfield roots (from Google's published
+// pki.goog/roots.pem) plus ISRG Root X1 (Let's Encrypt) and DigiCert
+// Global Root CA. Verified 2026-07-20 to validate the full chains of
+// api.anthropic.com, api.openai.com, generativelanguage.googleapis.com,
+// and script.google.com / *.googleapis.com. Roots are stable for years;
+// refresh from the same sources if a provider ever changes issuers.
